ModTrap: notices
================

ModTrap is our own code under the MIT licence (LICENSE).

1. Programs ModTrap calls and never contains
--------------------------------------------

- Mod Organizer 2 (GPL-3.0). ModTrap starts the owner's own installed copy from its command line and reads the
  instance's text files. No MO2 code is copied or bundled.
- xEdit / SSEEdit (MPL-2.0). ModTrap starts the owner's own installed copy, through MO2, with ModTrap's own script.
  No xEdit code or script is copied or bundled; ModTrap's script (modtrap/xedit/ModTrap.pas) is our own, written
  from scratch against xEdit's scripting functions, under ModTrap's MIT licence.

2. Code reused from the owner's other projects
----------------------------------------------

- tools/workplan (wp, the section index of the documents): taken from the owner's EldenNet (MIT), tools/workplan
  there, itself adapted from the workplan tool in the owner's Skyrizz. ModTrap's document list and codes replace
  EldenNet's.

- modtrap/server.py (the local page server: the Host, Origin and token checks, the response headers and content
  policy, the page's assembly): taken from the owner's DataPiler (MIT), datapiler/server.py there, with ModTrap's
  token header, page files and log, and without DataPiler's upload paths.

Planned, not yet taken: DataPiler's updater and its Windows launcher. Each is listed here when it lands, with the
file it came from. ModTrap's log (modtrap/logbook.py) follows DataPiler's idea of a numbered, masked ring of
lines, and is our own code.

3. Dependencies
---------------

None. The plan is the Python standard library only.

4. Mods
-------

No mod file, plugin or part of one is in this repository or in any release. Test fixtures are tiny plugins written
by ModTrap's own test code, with invented names and contents.
